The workflow for rebasing this fork onto a new upstream release existed only in
conversation, which is exactly where it gets lost. Put it in the README (both
languages) and ship the script it references.

- `scripts/sync-upstream.sh`: fetch upstream → rebase → per-file conflict hints
  → install + check:ci + pack → push with --force-with-lease. The proxy, when
  needed, is injected into individual git commands via DSH_GIT_PROXY; no global
  git/shell config is written and no credential is stored.
- README: one-time remote setup, the script path, the manual path, the
  patch-replay path for when documentation conflicts pile up, a table of which
  files conflict and what each resolution means, and the install step — with the
  reminder that removing the old package first matters because the plugin id is
  fixed.
